{%- comment -%}
  Elegant Moments drop-ship order email — body for the Shopify Flow
  "Send internal email" action.

  Paste everything below the SUBJECT block into the action's message body.
  SETUP.md has the rest of the workflow: trigger, conditions, sender, and the
  tag that stops an order being sent twice.

  ── The style number is DATA, not a derivation ───────────────────────────────

  It comes from the variant metafield custom.supplier_style, written by
  scripts/backfill-supplier-style.py from the STYLE column of the supplier's own
  liveinventory.csv.

  Do not be tempted to derive it from the SKU. The Phase 7 research proposed
  `sku | split: "-" | first`, and that is wrong for 466 of our 1,522 live
  variants (31%):

      SKU          that rule gives   actual supplier STYLE
      L1249BL      L1249BL           L1249      trailing colour code
      L2316P       L2316P            L2316
      L2316XP      L2316XP           L2316X     the X IS style, the P is not
      L1237SALE    L1237SALE         L1237
      82509        82509             85209      supplier's own transposition

  L2316P -> L2316 but L2316XP -> L2316X. A trailing letter is sometimes part of
  the style and sometimes a colour code, and nothing in the SKU distinguishes
  them. No string rule exists. Neither does the product title work: 220 of 673
  titles name a style number that no orderable variant actually has.

  If the metafield is ever empty the block below prints a DO NOT SHIP line
  rather than a guess. A visible stall is recoverable; a wrong garment in a
  discreet unmarked parcel is not.

  ── Why colour and size come from selectedOptions ────────────────────────────

  Not from variant.title. Colours like "Black/Red" and sizes like "O/S" and
  "1X/2X" both contain slashes, so "Black/Red / Q/S" cannot be split on "/"
  unambiguously. The fallback splits on " / " (space-slash-space), which IS
  safe: no option value in the catalogue contains that sequence, verified
  across all 127 distinct values by render_test.py.

  ── Formatting ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Dot leaders rather than column alignment, deliberately. If Flow renders the
  body as HTML, runs of spaces collapse and a padded table loses its columns;
  literal dots survive. A person keys this into an order-entry screen field by
  field, so one labelled field per line beats a table either way.

  STYLE and SIZE sit on separate lines so "2987X" can never be read as
  "style 2987, size X".
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} ═══ SUBJECT LINE (paste into Flow's Subject field) ═══════════
Drop-ship order {{ order.name }} — Velvet Tide
{%- endcomment -%}

DROP SHIP ORDER — VELVET TIDE
Our order reference: {{ order.name }}
{% comment %}
  A variable, not a literal, because this repo is PUBLIC on GitHub and the
  account number is what identifies us to the supplier's billing.

  In Flow: type the number directly into this line in the action body — Flow
  workflows are not stored in the repo.
  For manual sends: render_order.py supplies it from order_config.json, which
  is gitignored.

  The opening tag here deliberately has no leading hyphen: a whitespace-
  stripping open would swallow the newline that ends the line above and run the
  reference and the account number together. The closing tag does strip, to
  remove the newline this comment would otherwise leave behind.

  Do not write Liquid tag delimiters inside a comment body — naming the closing
  tag in prose ends the comment early and silently deletes the line below.
{% endcomment -%}
Dropship account: {{ account | default: "«ACCOUNT NUMBER — type it here in Flow; order_config.json for manual sends»" }}

Please ship the items below directly to the customer.
Bill the card we hold on file. Do not include a packing list.

============================================================
ITEMS
============================================================
{% for li in order.lineItems %}
{%- comment -%}
  Captured before the selectedOptions loop below. Liquid restores the outer
  forloop on endfor, but reading forloop.index after a nested loop is a subtle
  dependency and this costs nothing to make explicit.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign itemNo = forloop.index -%}
{%- assign sku = li.sku | strip -%}
{%- assign style = li.variant.metafields.custom.supplier_style | strip -%}
{%- assign colorValue = "" -%}
{%- assign sizeValue = "" -%}
{%- for opt in li.variant.selectedOptions -%}
  {%- if opt.name == "Color" -%}{%- assign colorValue = opt.value -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- if opt.name == "Size" -%}{%- assign sizeValue = opt.value -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Fallback if Flow does not expose selectedOptions on the line-item variable.
  Order is Color then Size, matching how the products were built; verified that
  variant.title is exactly the option values joined by " / " for all 1,522 live
  variants.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if colorValue == "" and sizeValue == "" -%}
  {%- assign parts = li.variant.title | split: " / " -%}
  {%- assign colorValue = parts[0] -%}
  {%- assign sizeValue = parts[1] -%}
{%- endif -%}
  ITEM {{ itemNo }}
{% if style == "" %}    STYLE ....... ** MISSING — DO NOT SHIP THIS LINE, WE WILL FOLLOW UP **
{% else %}    STYLE ....... {{ style }}
{% endif %}    COLOR ....... {{ colorValue | default: "—" }}
{% if sizeValue == "" %}    SIZE ........ One size (no size option on this item)
{% else %}    SIZE ........ {{ sizeValue }}
{% endif %}    QTY ......... {{ li.quantity }}
    (our ref: {{ li.product.title }} / SKU {{ sku | default: "—" }})
{% endfor %}
============================================================
SHIP TO
============================================================

    NAME ........ {{ order.shippingAddress.firstName }} {{ order.shippingAddress.lastName }}
{% if order.shippingAddress.company != blank %}    COMPANY ..... {{ order.shippingAddress.company }}
{% endif %}    ADDRESS ..... {{ order.shippingAddress.address1 }}
{% if order.shippingAddress.address2 != blank %}                  {{ order.shippingAddress.address2 }}
{% endif %}    CITY ........ {{ order.shippingAddress.city }}
    STATE ....... {{ order.shippingAddress.provinceCode }}
    ZIP ......... {{ order.shippingAddress.zip }}
    COUNTRY ..... {{ order.shippingAddress.countryCodeV2 }}
    PHONE ....... {{ order.shippingAddress.phone | default: "not provided" }}

============================================================

Ship method: Standard.
Tracking: please reply to this email with the tracking number and carrier.

If any item is unavailable, reply and tell us which. Please HOLD the whole
order until we confirm — do not part-ship, and do not substitute.

{% comment %}
  Deliberately not "sent automatically" — render_order.py sends this same
  template by hand until the Flow workflow is live, and the wording has to be
  true in both cases.

  Non-stripping open, stripping close, for the whitespace reason explained at
  the account line above.
{% endcomment -%}
This order has been sent once. If you receive it twice, the second copy is an
error: ship reference {{ order.name }} only once.

Velvet Tide
